Third-party software this project uses, and the licences it comes under:

* **Firecracker** — <https://github.com/firecracker-microvm/firecracker> — Apache-2.0, by Amazon
  Web Services and its contributors.  It is the hypervisor every run uses, and it is used as a
  **released binary**: this project does not modify it, and `make download` fetches a release of it.
  Its source, its licence and its notice are in the repository above.
* The **guest's userland** (`make rootfs`) is assembled from Debian's own packages, each under its
  own licence; the full text of each is inside the image, under `/usr/share/doc/*/copyright`.  The
  Firefox ESR, VLC and Python builds are packaged the same way.
* The **guest's framebuffer module** (`desktop-cracker/guest-kernel/`) is built against the Linux
  kernel's interfaces and carries its own `SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0`, which is what a Linux
  kernel module declares; it is the one part of this tree that is not MIT.
